<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German Olympic Committee names Munich as bid city choice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d55b6cc42e6c42d0caf27ba3b1ce7f5aec252e0a19ec53b0654a2b38d741add</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284--424a4614f81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich has been voted as the city that will bid for the Olympics in 2036, 2040 or 2044. Berlin had been in the running but withdrew on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Propaganda in Russian schools prepares students to die</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88bd737f1f813c6fee86ca89052644f5255a06d801e3ba2ce0cbc8014d6431b9</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/propaganda-in-russian-schools-prepares-students-to-die/a-79417294--eaf06d603c17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/propaganda-in-russian-schools-prepares-students-to-die/a-79417294?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian government wants children to learn about patriotism from an early age. DW spoke to students in Siberia about their views on propaganda, the war in Ukraine and their future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Paris: Pope Leo XIV to celebrate Mass before huge crowd</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d89cca3ab863fc6f13fc358b68072dd813937e6656fa0de06fe8b2412a941b63</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T11:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-to-celebrate-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864--12fea0a34da9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-to-celebrate-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Around 600,000 people have registered to attend a Mass at the Place de la Concorde, near the Champs-Elysees. Pope Leo XIV is on a four-day visit to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b83a32685da5b1ac1a4b172e691a08811e7c2045f80ebc6d82f20b980a04ab2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Deadly blast rips through Athens building, near Acropolis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab118c7db5d268a92ddcc6fe2efdcf721f38e53224b8d6afffc4b252225382b3</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deadly-blast-rips-through-athens-building-near-acropolis/a-79441931--87a5e1705efa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deadly-blast-rips-through-athens-building-near-acropolis/a-79441931?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several foreign tourists remain missing after an explosion brought down a building in Athens' tourist area of Plaka, with the city's mayor calling it an "incredible disaster."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: EU ministers meet for migration showdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6296a2c8622d6fbbb1a2c49bf5bab69b34d0c1cb24180a59e981fa598f9f863</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-eu-ministers-meet-for-migration-showdown/live-79441034--691a60120f40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-eu-ministers-meet-for-migration-showdown/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European interior ministers hold migration talks in Munich as the bloc plans to strengthen borders and speed up deportations. Also, will Cologne or Munich win the battle to bid for the Olympic Games? DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi, Islamabad trade accusations at UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:113fd8609c3c3be0732f8372101e41102d149ebeb186c8117130ec8656cb5318</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-islamabad-trade-accusations-at-un-general-assembly/live-79440869--5c329050c900.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-islamabad-trade-accusations-at-un-general-assembly/live-79440869?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shehbaz Sharif criticized India's policy on Kashmir and praised Pakistan's military, while New Delhi accused Islamabad of supporting cross-border terrorism. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Thailand: Bangkok flooding triggers disaster declaration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28455b15da59a14b5db5ed0e0e5da4b9edeaa3526e43c35e46ea20e6639151ef</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575--24f35b64d6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rainfall over the past three days has caused heavy flooding in the Thai capital. A state of disaster has been declared in all 50 districts in Bangkok.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI tools post user images from ChatGPT online</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4a08483d27e3154e6f0c3ff09085e7f2a0c5238a3b176e7c2ff7700b77a6eef</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/openai-tools-post-user-images-from-chatgpt-online/a-79440406--854a7e11bf2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/openai-tools-post-user-images-from-chatgpt-online/a-79440406?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI said it found 53 cases in which user-uploaded image links on ChatGPT were shared with third-party websites. The company said it had removed most of these links.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House bars CNN from covering upcoming Trump trip, broadcaster says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8472c3a3d33a5e5ed2d3aeeed55e1688a36b52122a3a7147b159af254a8766e2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T03:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-bars-cnn-from-covering-upcoming-trump-trip-broadcaster-says/a-79440241--597a83f39a01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-bars-cnn-from-covering-upcoming-trump-trip-broadcaster-says/a-79440241?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CNN said its journalists have been barred from accompanying President Donald Trump on his upcoming trip to Tennessee. The episode marks the Trump administration's latest salvo against the major cable news network.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>TikTok agrees to settle with Alabama state over teen safety</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d20ce29e553d88fe2e8f5fc75f476e2cf54d4c3d0af17d2d83d4010eb2287c</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T03:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tiktok-agrees-to-settle-with-alabama-state-over-teen-safety/a-79440240--8af3dd0cef0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tiktok-agrees-to-settle-with-alabama-state-over-teen-safety/a-79440240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The settlement involves TikTok adding several child safety measures to its platform including time limits and increased parental control. It is similar to a recent settlement competitor Meta had reached.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemeni leader calls for general mobilization against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd66b9825b2fad7a194c6acc8aa2d7bb879c0eecca9a8051769c64f74c4fec8d</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T21:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemeni-leader-calls-for-general-mobilization-against-houthis/a-79439604--0bc1a71d540c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemeni-leader-calls-for-general-mobilization-against-houthis/a-79439604?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid military escalation with the Iran-backed Houthis, the Saudi-backed head of Yemen's governing body urged his compatriots to join the government forces.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lula or Bolsonaro as president? Brazil gears up to vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd4a3238225d084ef8259e8143c97fdac38f0667e5564435f51065c03d969cb3</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276--a6f357f68a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilians go to the polls on October 4. The front-runners are multilateralist incumbent Lula da Silva and former President Jair Bolsonaro's son, Flavio, who wants to bring Brazil closer to the US and away from China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament approves fuel tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c654d4ae291548e40741e6fad2ec9104b7353381b357771deb5d3128acc6f6a5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T19:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882--bd35c461e842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers hope to drive down fuel prices by cutting taxes on gas and diesel from October 1. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister visited Budapest to ramp up defense and military ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian President Pezeshkian brought a diplomatic tone to New York for UNGA. What did his remarks signal?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b4395afa605f9c8a79d4e7d6344cc217dd885968f894fc677819a64cd6c09df</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-sig/a-79428890--b543693f4fe7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-signal/a-79428890?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's president used his trip to New York this week for the UN General Assembly to signal openness to talks over the nuclear dispute. However, the chances of a major breakthrough on the war remain low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan's Sharif rails against India, praises Trump at UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddc824197aeee97ed158a74cf05af89e2ae9d742694f3be3eb6a1025b20a58b8</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-sharif-rails-against-india-praises-trump-at-unga/live-79366211--e466853c3946.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-sharif-rails-against-india-praises-trump-at-unga/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's prime minister blamed India for last year's clashes, and credited the US president with preventing "all-out war" between two nuclear powers. Albania's PM told the UN delegates an anecdote about AI misuse.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DW shows solidarity with Georgians' commitment to democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41b2e866a3b2f6beeef993d5b0ad1e9dcb597436a0fc1f31abcb007c1c257af5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731--f6945c635292.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cultural and media professionals in Georgia remain under threat. A DW panel brings together insiders who share their hopes and fears.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Xi wraps up US visit with trip to National Archives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bf5e3a036c6f758ddc087641106474dce765f3a060a1fd85bce9f15fbc062a4</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/xi-wraps-up-us-visit-with-trip-to-national-archives/live-79404511--6f3b43dc50d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/xi-wraps-up-us-visit-with-trip-to-national-archives/live-79404511?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the last day of his visit to the US, Chinese leader Xi Jinping visited the National Archives with President Donald Trump. The Archives store the Declaration of Independence and the US Constitution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD, CDU ban new Holocaust 'stumbling stones' in Heidenau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3507f7d5b759ad4177b695bf9a3719319e00e6ec9b195e3dcde45a3035a6d202</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919--bafd061ca07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Activists, politicians and representatives of Holocaust victims reacted with anger after the center-right CDU party joined forces with the AfD to ban new Stolpersteine (stumbling stones) in the eastern town of Heidenau.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Lithuanian skies are NATO skies': DW speaks with Lithuanian premier Mindaugas Sinkevicius</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bf4a0e812acd03d84393a4533fcff1c718c2fc0888c38e6a422965f7e13da64</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394--2e48449cf03c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a DW interview, Prime Minister Mindaugas Sinkevicius discussed threats to Lithuania from Russia and Belarus, NATO's need for stronger air defense and why military spending alone cannot ensure security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e27de098ada8de987cd5e42807cba93ef738884c407fff6b5515b67b5fdd4ceb</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717--3029f0ff55b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundesliga and three other leading European football leagues have said major reforms to world-governing body FIFA are "essential." However, they stopped short of calling for the resignation of boss Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How Bulgaria become a global leader in battery storage and what this means for the country's grid and energy market?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16d20e804a876c6456e23be47830d4fe8cc2d359862b2aecb6bf032c1e5d376f</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-an/a-79428289--917b8ba9c523.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-and-energy-market/a-79428289?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In under two years, Bulgaria has become one of the world's most battery-intensive energy markets. Can the surge last — and what will it mean for conventional power generators?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy to ban burqa in schools, limit foreign pupils</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:451b1d22bda96ea2f37baf3e819f4175c9c6c94137755d966401db01a8ac1f62</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432--d459be98ca4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni’s government has passed new school rules capping the number of students who don't speak fluent Italian and banning face coverings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffff30ea64415990be67f46843361dc3355000d1215bf9f4e7e433e5f6a0fffd</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00b1c0565d047241e68794c4dd6cf9c104e42672929b33560104f20087b18f5a</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86552b8edd8f6a3242b3c14abf719449139599bcc24774ea84a01608cf9385bd</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but re