-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage sites are far less full than in recent years. Officials say supplies are secure, but analysts warn that a cold winter or import disruptions could push prices higher. So how secure is the supply?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: VW to step up cost-cutting program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fb79fbccda37aa75cd7ad0f1add3ef541fa0c058a449cff96d913e2ae687fd5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190--a755a3e03dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen's chief says the carmaker will accelerate its streamlining measures as workers protest. The Israeli ambassador says the Left Party win in Berlin polls poses a risk to the city's Jewish community. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How will Germany's Merz respond after crushing state election results and losses to the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ecc004d69f0c30832a46b9f04161d15f56d83f9d6df8d4e023fbd4088115667</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-will-germany-s-merz-respond-after-crushing-state-election-results-and-losses-to-the-far-right/a-79365325--120a3b5033f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-will-germany-s-merz-respond-after-crushing-state-election-results-and-losses-to-the-far-right/a-79365325?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD and the socialist Left Party gained ground in recent state elections, while the centrist parties lost support. The biggest loser is Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Princess Diana's brother makes explosive claims about royals in new memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d395ee42fd453667784e292fd314a7ed21d45c7426977f9f6cfadf6bb3c93358</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465--3d900d102240.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Here are some of the key revelations from Charles Earl Spencer's highly anticipated memoir "Swan Song: Diana, My Sister." It has already provoked Buckingham Palace to react.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Trial starts of ex-Transport Minister Scheuer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06321eddd004263cdb2bc3b5ab3ab03cbabf786380ebec8e877cdf03df1d3c86</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160--5052118e7b45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Transport Minister Andreas Scheuer is being tried for perjury related to a failed car toll scheme. And cherry farmers have brought in a bumper harvest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d38c45a96542605fac2ee0cd8b7e8f381ef45c49d07c8ef98c6621ff24ff8ad2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75713001aa21a3825f6c42e644aeb193cb2c9a292d54f70b363503024e910f77</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD makes gains in state elections but has no government options</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:276d45c0853b7cca331a786b7470a8e73c4433eb480c0bba063e612b4b09c244</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T19:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308--1a6e760f93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite making significant gains in both Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the far-right AfD remains without options to form a state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9755d39710fc28bf53e48f48d6e8b707f1d8c1b337d052ef9cd95046356342d7</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dccb9f9734f264d88d10a936efa5cfe4d374a58234188bc434affaceb5c4bb44</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09bc007032f013c2b8b0d73482aa39e64b27eedb4c8fdcd3b47c13ba0439cfef</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest 2026 is underway but it's not just beer on offer in Munich this year; revelers can also get themselves a flu jab before heading to the tents. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d4f5a38c2600fd52e687a522ac2e8bc5549b54a7efbf7393c6e933a556ee32c</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Summer of 2026 broke records in Europe, and caused deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fa1d1f82c17ca9e3ac7319095dc9884f0a265bdf3cf68cef5d9cde6284ce0a1</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630--5efe97f5474b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was not only the hottest on record in Europe, it also saw a record number of people die. More than 16,000 are thought to have died because of the heat in Germany alone.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>German-Russian relations at freezing point</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4746ce502169e98b41555bbcb84c066c4c42ce4f5b180558606aa6869891a2e</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741--08a579f047c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine destroyed the once-close relationship between Moscow and Berlin. Yet the far-right AfD is calling for a normalization of relations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine steps up measures to protect railways</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0fe29c7401def52cdf3e5e12aa99e26168b1c4bea09a5751f037389ef5855d0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087--356ca60a409d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia increases its attacks on Ukraine's rail infrastructure, the Ukrainian government has called for help to replace destroyed locomotives and is making plans to keep passengers safe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: Will economy shape the vote?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55521758e7804a0a28a8a55e4d72d8b86a1b12e8af250ffcdb0de63217d9807</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904--432385452f89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters in the eastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania head to the polls on Sunday, with the Social Democrats and far-right AfD neck and neck. Here's a look at key economic issues that could influence the election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ac6e21a14196946084ac027ac1ab556095261f5e2cb3d72402cef5a61a7ec</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Rebels, workers, radicals: The making of 'Red Berlin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbceeff11d2703d69c2b6bbc4079877a81e021f23a20a76d52bd2457cbcefbed</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: SPD seeks to fend off AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6569aa0391b57be21125f74558c0dd23124f968dc3a04df050eae348a6b4cb95</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234--336ea67c69c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For nearly three decades, the Social Democrats have governed Germany's northeastern state. If they can fend off the AfD, the result may boost the fortunes of the German government's junior coalition partner.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:335ee95ab3c4c8adfcfc8995ec4fa347912c1e76e808b823c89f5b459203c9c0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ea10f43316743f98511babd761d8e3d4895445a968d33513bb342b953aa6ac</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d6140c91c3e224d977291a5cd5b7d18cce82acae8149d025a3015b3c06cead</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7277ff7ef578fb9e8f92bebd9f2e8122002de4d696d3b67207701cfde57dee53</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU: A look at the bloc's special relationships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae49cbedb8c408cf53481a2ea757820526de3288879864f8a0f66bd32f8e1381</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797--41616c65f5bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Canada may be some distance from Europe geographically, closer political ties are in the cards. With talk of an associate membership, DW takes a look at other arrangements the EU has with particular countries.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0537129a1a04fb2bfbc4497964f14a0827b2bf0ad86f39b773c4aed178eff4b5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0e11fd1940a0da2ce3a14a8920938fb6a4e4ac4696d383360bc2eee764e6e7</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e0298b1f33e7ad2dbb604d79367a5bb28c2e082cde2b3da1e3bf3808b648f8</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0ca1b22cdd993d2c89e0372dd38c5143740a45aa720ba51c3ae940355a561ff</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03cfbe1b05944acd539d9484eed3637c7e797de63853e23bf42b605f5f0e82b5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4c46c5606767961d04084a8c3a48ae92f8a588705857c417c40b18a55547aa</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a46516d9fbeb9031e0a8c3e39c60d30dcc7992f9b06f8f4f4b4292